From f36ed24503855ba5dd67a9083bef2779fff65ec3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:49:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 31/33] drm/gma500: schedule sgxfive transfer jobs with
 drm_sched

Add one drm_sched scheduler for the device and an entity per transfer
context, so a context's jobs reach the firmware in order. Running a job
copies its firmware command into the context's client CCB, advances the
write offset, creates its hardware fence and queues the firmware's transfer
work for the context. A job that times out marks its context lost and fails
its fences; firmware recovery comes later. The credit limit keeps queued
commands inside one context's CCB. Nothing submits jobs yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
